<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#fetchedAt> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://w3id.org/iprok/signal> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#rainfallMM> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Daily rainfall in millimetres at the project's GPS coordinates. Used by the auto-risk engine to gate monsoon triggers." .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#weekOfYear> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#LabourSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#ExternalSignal> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#HistoricalWeatherProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "10-year climatology snapshot at a project's GPS; 52 weekly buckets, each with avg rainfall + rain probability + extreme-heat probability. Source: NASA POWER (power.larc.nasa.gov), free climatology API, no auth required. Fetched once at project geocoding; treated as static climate context (re-fetch only if site GPS changes)." .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#heatProbability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Empirical probability [0, 1] that this calendar week sees at least one day with max temp > 40°C, computed across the 10 years of the climatology window. Indian-summer concrete-pour productivity drops sharply above 40°C." .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#pricePerUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "market price per unit (INR)" .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#weekOfYear> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "week of year" .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#volatility30d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#LabourSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Per-week per-state labour availability score (0-1, where 0 = peak festival/harvest absence). Reason field carries the cause: Diwali / Pongal / Kharif harvest / Normal. Source: calendarific.com API + ICAR crop calendar." .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#fetchedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "profile fetched at" .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#workingDayLossRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "working day loss risk" .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#pricePerUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#WeatherSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Daily weather snapshot at a project's GPS; rainfall, max temp, working-day-loss-risk. Source: IMD via indianapi.in (free tier) with OpenWeatherMap fallback." .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#sourceYears> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#rainfallMM> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#rainfallMM> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://bimsaarthi.com/ontology/v0/rainfallMM> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#workingDayLossRisk> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://w3id.org/iprok/signal> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#WeatherSignal> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://w3id.org/iprok/signal> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#availabilityScore> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Score in [0, 1]. 0 = peak festival absence (Diwali week, Pongal week, Kharif harvest); 1 = normal availability. <0.5 triggers the festival_labour_shortage auto-risk." .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#HistoricalWeatherWeek> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://bimsaarthi.com/ontology/v0/HistoricalWeatherWeek> .
<https://w3id.org/iprok/signal#fetchedAt> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://bimsaarthi.com/ontology/v0/fetchedAt> .
